  "Id": 2470,
  "Title": "AKU's First Paediatric Boot Camp",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "The Paediatric Boot Camp was conducted to provide simulation-based hands-on training to improve novice airway providers' skills and confidence in a challenging but safe learning environment.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The Paediatric Boot Camp was conducted by the Department of Paediatrics & Child Health in collaboration with CIME to provide simulation-based hands-on training to improve novice airway providers' skills and confidence in a challenging but safe learning environment. A total of 17 paediatric residents, fellows and nurses participated. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "High fidelity simulation scenarios were included in this camp such as Intubating a neonate with a seizure disorder, displaced endotracheal/tracheostomy tube, upper airway obstruction, and anterior mediastinal mass-difficult airway anticipation. These highly realistic scenarios helped prepare learners to deal with airway management cases in high-pressure, high-risk environments."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "We aim to reach many more staff through a series of boot camps, using the \"the train to success\" concept with repetitive practice."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
